<br />files !!![/center][/size][/b][center]﻿[/center]
<br />This is a mod that works with the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/11398]Farmer Portraits[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/18384]Fashion Sense Outfits[/url] frameworks to change your farmer's outfits/looks day to day automatically. (Conversely, it requires both of those and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/9969]Fashion Sense[/url] to be installed).
<br />
<br />[b]Features:
<br />[/b]- full config that will allow you to set up which features you will and will not be using;
<br />- randomization between multiple outfits;
<br />- indoor and maternity postfixes denoting versions of each outfit to wear indoors and/or when pregnant;
<br />- multi-save functionality that lets you load up any save and as long as the config matches, the correct portraits (and outfits, that's intristic to that framework) will be selected automatically;
<br />- a base outfit/portrait that will be active when none of the others are;
<br />- pajamas that your farmer may wear inside the farmhouse in the morning and/or in the evening, for a configurable duration, now with a seasonal version;
<br />- a raincoat that your farmer may wear when it's raining;
<br />- alternatively, seasonal raincoats for your farmer to wear in different seasons;
<br />- seasonal outfits that your farmer will change into as the seasons change;
<br />- a mining outfit to wear in the mines, the quarry cave, the skull cavern and the volcano, with an option for seasonal variation as well;
<br />- a desert outfit and an island outfit to wear in the Calico Desert and on the Ginger island;
<br />- a pirate outfit for all your pirate party needs;
<br />- festival and wedding outfits that your farmer will change into on the appropriate day (when they're out of their pajamas anyway :) ),
<br />- bathhouse outfit with easy to set up custom location support;
<br />- relatively easy to set up custom festival support;
<br />- Downtown Zuzu, East Scarp, Walk to Desert Redux, Desert Afforestation Area and Cape Stardew support for mining and desert outfits.
<br />
<br />[b][size=4][url=https://file-metadata.nexusmods.com/file/nexus-readmes/1303/19503/readme.txt]See the readme file for detailed tutorials on how to set up the mod for use.[/url][/size][/b]
<br />
<br />[center][b][size=6]﻿UPDATED FOR 1.6[/size][/b][/center]
<br />[b]Known issues:[/b]
<br />- when loading a save, the farmer will wake up in the same outfit they went to bed in, and will stay in it until either time or location (i.e. you go to the cellar or leave the farmhouse) changes, prompting an update. Going to bed and waking up while continuously playing will have the outfit change on wakeup appropriately. Wearing pajamas in the morning and evening and always going to bed late enough to be wearing pajamas will make the issue invisible;
<br />- if your config has your game try to change you into an outfit that isn't in your Fashion Sense wardrobe / portrait folder, it won't change you into anything at all. Make sure to set up your config correctly for your wardrobe!
<br />- not having the default portrait.png file in your farmer's portraits folder will cause the entire portrait functionality to fail to work (and possibly the entire mod, I haven't tested that yet). Even if you're using seasonal outfits so you'll never see the default portrait, you have to have the file;
<br />- in Fashion Sense, if you change from an outfit that has accessories into an outfit that doesn't have a single one, accessories will carry over. This is nifty and convenient for something like elf ears, less so for a raincoat or a winter scarf. Add a choker or something for each outfit (or just your pajamas) to prevent this;
<br />- in Farmer Portraits 1.6, only 64x64 portraits work.
<br />
<br />Either of the halves of the mod can be disabled individually (in which case you won't need the corresponding framework to necessarily be installed), or you can use my standalone [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/19497]portrait mod[/url] and/or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/19502]outfit mod[/url] instead :)
